<title>SOUTH KOREA: Swiss Bank Corp clarifies Asiana deal.</title>
<headline>Swiss Bank Corp clarifies Asiana deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swiss Bank Corp on Friday denied it had taken an equity stake in South Korea's Asiana Airlines.</p>
<p>Camille Yeh, the bank's Hong Kong-based regional head of corporate communications, said SBC Warburg had simply arranged the purchase of a 19.02 percent stake in the airline by Malaysian-based Pacific Investment Capital Ltd.</p>
<p>She denied Pacific Investment was a Swiss Bank entity, as reported on Wednesday by Asiana and South Korean government officials.</p>
</text>
